  <div class="fcx" aria-label="Dry/Wet Scrubbers Manufacturers in Assam">
<section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-duo"><div class="fcx-panel"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-circle-question"></i></span><h2>What Are Dry and Wet Scrubbers?</h2><p>Scrubbers are air-pollution control systems used to remove unwanted pollutants from exhaust streams before the treated air is discharged. The two primary approaches are dry scrubbing and wet scrubbing.</p><p>Dry Scrubbers use absorbent materials or chemical reactions to remove pollutants without using water. They are especially useful for acidic gases, high-temperature exhaust, and industrial emission-control applications.</p><p>Wet Scrubbers use liquid solutions or water sprays to capture and neutralize pollution. They may be used for fumes, grease, oil, and other contaminants depending on the application.</p></div><div class="fcx-panel"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-filter"></i></span><h2>Dry Scrubbers</h2><p>Dry scrubbers are designed to extract harmful gases and particulates from exhaust streams. They are normally used for controlling acidic gases and can handle high-temperature and highly acidic exhaust conditions.</p><p>The Assam range includes FAEK-1, FAEK-2, FAEK-3, and FAEK-4 models. A single unit can handle capacity up to 12,000 CFM, while multiple systems can offer maximum capacity up to 60,000 CFM.</p><p>Dry scrubbers may be selected for different industrial processes depending on the type of pollutant and required exhaust treatment.</p></div><div class="fcx-panel" style="grid-column:1/-1"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-filter"></i></span><h2>Wet Scrubbers</h2><p>Wet scrubbers use liquid sprays to capture contaminants from exhaust air. In kitchen applications, fumes are drawn through hoods and passed through high-pressure water jets, which trap contaminants such as oil and grease before cleaner air is exhausted.</p><p>The FanAir wet scrubber is designed for high scrubbing efficiency with very low pressure drop. Its construction includes an aluminium profile frame, heavy-gauge base, double-skin or single-skin casing, spray headers, centrifugal blowers, motors, pumps, and a sump arrangement.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band fcx-band--alt"><div class="fcx-wrap"><h2>Wet Scrubber Construction</h2><p>The wet scrubber construction includes various components designed for reliable operation:</p><ul class="fcx-checks"><li><b>Frame:</b> Extruded aluminium profile</li><li><b>Base:</b> Heavy-gauge base frame with cast aluminium corners</li><li><b>Casing:</b> 23+2 mm double-skin panels using 0.6 mm sheets with PUF insulation, or 1.6/1.8 mm GI single-skin construction</li><li><b>Wet Section:</b> Double-bank GI spray header with brass/PVC spray nozzles</li><li><b>Blowers:</b> DIDW centrifugal blowers</li><li><b>Motors:</b> TEFC three-phase motors</li><li><b>Motor Stand:</b> Adjustable motor mounting fixture</li><li><b>Pulleys:</b> Adjustable taper bush pulleys</li><li><b>Pumps:</b> Standard monoblock pumps</li><li><b>Sump:</b> SS304/GI with FRP tank and water overflow/drain connections</li></ul><p>These components are configured according to the requirements of the wet scrubbing application.</p></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><h2>Key Features of Dry/Wet Scrubbers</h2><p>The main features of the scrubber range include:</p><ul class="fcx-checks"><li>Industrial pollution control</li><li>Dry and wet scrubbing configurations</li><li>Removal of gases and particulates</li><li>Suitable for acidic gas treatment</li><li>High-temperature exhaust handling for dry scrubbers</li><li>High scrubbing performance in wet systems</li><li>Low pressure drop in wet scrubber applications</li><li>Multiple dry scrubber models</li><li>Single and multi-unit capacity options</li><li>DIDW centrifugal blowers in wet scrubbers</li><li>TEFC 3-phase motors</li><li>Corrosion-resistant material options for selected components</li></ul><p>The final scrubber configuration should be selected according to the pollutant type, airflow, pressure, temperature, and application.</p></div></section><section class="fcx-band fcx-band--alt"><div class="fcx-wrap"><h2>Technical Specifications</h2><div class="fcx-tables fcx-tables--2"><div class="fcx-tablewrap"><h3>Dry Scrubber</h3><table class="fcx-table"><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Product</th><td>Dry Scrubber</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Models</th><td>FAEK-1, FAEK-2, FAEK-3, FAEK-4</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Single Unit Capacity</th><td>Up to 12,000 CFM</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Multi-Unit Capacity</th><td>Up to 60,000 CFM</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Main Function</th><td>Gas &amp; Particulate Removal</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Suitable For</th><td>Acidic &amp; High-Temperature Exhaust</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="fcx-tablewrap"><h3>Wet Scrubber</h3><table class="fcx-table"><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Product</th><td>Wet Scrubber</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Frame</th><td>Extruded Aluminium Profile</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Base</th><td>Heavy-Gauge Base Frame</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Casing</th><td>Double Skin / Single Skin GI</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Insulation</th><td>PUF, 38+2 kg/cu. m density</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Wet Section</th><td>Double Bank GI Spray Header</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Spray Nozzles</th><td>Brass / PVC</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Blowers</th><td>DIDW Centrifugal Blowers</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Motors</th><td>TEFC, Three Phase</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Pumps</th><td>Monoblock Pumps</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Sump</th><td>SS304/GI with FRP Tank</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class="fcx-note fcx-note--wide"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-sliders"></i></span><div><p>These specifications are based on the current Assam scrubber product page. Final sizing and configuration should be determined from the actual airflow, static pressure, pollutant characteristics, and application requirements.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-center"><h2>Applications of Dry/Wet Scrubbers</h2></div><div class="fcx-cards fcx-cards--3"><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-industry"></i></span><h3>Pharmaceutical Industries</h3><p>Pharmaceutical manufacturing processes can also generate fumes, gases, and particulates that require controlled exhaust treatment. Scrubbers may be selected according to the characteristics of the exhaust stream.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-industry"></i></span><h3>Chemical and Process Industries</h3><p>Chemical and process plants can produce acidic gases and other contaminants. Dry or wet scrubbing systems may be selected according to the pollutant and process conditions.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-industry"></i></span><h3>Textile Processing</h3><p>Textile processing applications can require exhaust treatment for process-related emissions. Scrubber selection depends on the type and concentration of contaminants.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-filter"></i></span><h3>Oil and Gas</h3><p>Oil and gas facilities may require specialised exhaust treatment for different process emissions. Proper system sizing is important for effective pollutant control.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-industry"></i></span><h3>Food Processing</h3><p>Food-processing facilities can use wet scrubbers for selected fumes, grease, and process exhaust applications.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-hotel"></i></span><h3>Kitchen Exhaust</h3><p>Wet scrubbers can capture oil and grease from cooking fumes using water spray systems before the treated air is discharged.</p><p>The current Assam page lists applications such as pharmaceuticals, textile processing, oil and gas, fertilizer manufacturing, wastewater treatment, metal processing, electronics, food processing, cocoa processing, asphalt processing, and kitchen/process exhaust treatment.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band fcx-band--alt"><div class="fcx-wrap"><h2>Benefits of Dry/Wet Scrubbers</h2><p>Properly selected scrubbers can provide several practical benefits:</p><ul class="fcx-checks"><li>Pollutant removal from industrial exhaust streams</li><li>Suitable for acidic gas treatment</li><li>Dry systems can operate without water</li><li>Wet systems can capture liquid-soluble contaminants</li><li>Suitable for high-temperature exhaust applications</li><li>Different capacity options</li><li>Low pressure drop in suitable wet scrubber applications</li><li>Suitable for commercial and industrial exhaust treatment</li><li>Multiple application possibilities</li><li>Can be designed according to project-specific requirements</li></ul><p>Actual pollution-control performance depends on pollutant characteristics, concentration, airflow, temperature, chemical properties, scrubber configuration, and operating conditions.</p></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-blocks"><div class="fcx-block"><h2>Dry/Wet Scrubbers Suppliers in Assam</h2><p><b>As Dry/Wet Scrubbers Suppliers in Assam</b>, we offer scrubber solutions for chemical, pharmaceutical, process, kitchen, and other exhaust treatment applications. The equipment may be selected according to airflow, static pressure, pollutant type, and site conditions.</p><p>Assam has a diverse industrial environment, including tea processing units across the Brahmaputra Valley, refineries, oil and gas installations, cement and food-processing facilities, hospitals, and commercial buildings. Heavy monsoon conditions and high humidity can also make corrosion-resistant construction and reliable ventilation critical considerations for many projects.</p><p>For Assam projects, an appropriate dry or wet scrubber configuration should be selected according to the exhaust characteristics and required treatment process.</p></div><div class="fcx-block"><h2>Dry/Wet Scrubber Manufacturer in India</h2><p>The scrubbers supplied for Assam projects are manufactured at the FanAir facility in Neemrana, Rajasthan. Each unit is selected according to the required airflow, static pressure, application, and site conditions.</p><p>Technical data and sizing support may be supplied before ordering. Finished equipment may be dispatched to project locations across Assam and other parts of India.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band fcx-band--alt"><div class="fcx-wrap"><h2>How to Choose the Right Scrubber</h2><p>Selecting the right scrubber requires understanding the entire exhaust-treatment requirement.</p><ul class="fcx-checks fcx-checks--long"><li><b>Identify the pollutant:</b> Determine whether the exhaust carries gases, particulates, oil, grease, fumes, or other contaminants.</li><li><b>Select the scrubber type:</b> Choose a dry or wet configuration according to the pollutant and treatment process.</li><li><b>Airflow:</b> Determine the required CFM or airflow volume.</li><li><b>Static pressure:</b> Consider ductwork and other system resistance.</li><li><b>Temperature:</b> Check the operating temperature of the exhaust stream.</li><li><b>Pollutant concentration:</b> Consider the quantity and characteristics of contaminants.</li><li><b>Material:</b> Select suitable construction materials according to the operating environment.</li><li><b>Capacity:</b> Select single or multiple units according to the specified airflow.</li><li><b>Site conditions:</b> Consider humidity, corrosion, installation area, and maintenance access.</li></ul><p>Providing accurate exhaust and process information helps in selecting a suitable pollution-control system.</p></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-center"><h2>FAQs</h2></div><div class="fcx-faq"><details><summary>What is a dry scrubber?</summary><p>A dry scrubber is pollution-control equipment that eliminates harmful gases and particulates from exhaust streams using absorbent materials or chemical reactions without using water.</p></details><details><summary>What is a wet scrubber?</summary><p>A wet scrubber uses liquid sprays or solutions to capture and neutralize pollution from an exhaust stream. It can also be used for kitchen fumes containing contaminants such as oil and grease.</p></details><details><summary>What is the capacity of the dry scrubber?</summary><p>The listed dry scrubber capacity is up to 12,000 CFM for a single unit and up to 60,000 CFM using multiple units.</p></details><details><summary>What models are available for dry scrubbers?</summary><p>The current range includes FAEK-1, FAEK-2, FAEK-3, and FAEK-4 models.</p></details><details><summary>Where are dry and wet scrubbers used?</summary><p>They are used across pharmaceutical, chemical, textile, oil and gas, fertilizer, wastewater treatment, metal, electronics, food-processing, kitchen exhaust, and other industrial applications.</p></details></div><div class="fcx-center" style="margin-top:26px"><a href="product.php" class="btn-cyber btn-cyber--primary fcx-btn" title="Fan Air India Products">Learn More <i class="fas fa-arrow-right"></i></a></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-cta"><h2>Conclusion</h2><p>Dry and wet scrubbers provide vital solutions for controlling pollutants in commercial and industrial exhaust systems. Dry scrubbers are appropriate for applications involving gases and particulates, such as acidic and high-temperature exhaust, while wet scrubbers use liquid sprays to capture and neutralize suitable contaminants.</p><p>FanAir India Pvt. Ltd. manufactures dry and wet scrubbers at its Neemrana facility and supplies them to Assam and other locations throughout India. Proper selection based on pollutant type, airflow, static pressure, temperature, application, and site conditions can help achieve an effective exhaust-treatment system.</p><a href="../contact.php" class="fcx-cta__btn" title="Contact Fan Air India">Contact Us <i class="fas fa-arrow-right"></i></a></div></div></section>
